ok thread new() does not run the capsule before start()
ok thread writes a shared object that main reads after join()
ok thread join() answers what the capsule handed back
ok thread wait() is join()'s second name
ok thread join() answers an object made on the thread
ok thread gets its own copy of a list: its copy grew to 3, the caller's stayed 2
ok thread two side by side each answer their own count
ok thread lock(): three threads adding to one field lose nothing
ok thread lock(): three threads appending to one list field lose nothing
ok thread runs an object's own capsule: thread.new(object.capsule())
ok thread on a capsule by bare name runs the subtype's replacement
ok thread started through one name, joined through the other
ok thread two names for one thread are ==
ok thread two threads are not ==, even running the same call
ok thread stop() ends a thread that never would, and it writes nothing after join()
ok thread displays before start() as (thread twice, not started)
ok thread displays after stop() as (thread forever, stopped)
